Return `false` from the `_.transform` callback to stop iteration early:

```js
const result = _.transform(collection, (accumulator, value, key) => {
  accumulator[key] = value;

  if (/* stop condition */) {
    return false;
  }
}, {});
```

The callback receives `(accumulator, value, key, collection)`. Mutate the accumulator; its return value is used to determine whether iteration continues. Returning `false` breaks the loop.
